{
  "schema": 1,
  "description": "Issue #4036 slice 7a: a feed's staged NDJSON rows and attributes in; what today's pfb_unbound_python_sources() writes (the manifest's feed rows and each .raw file's lines) and the DNSBL widget counts per group, and what go/pfb_core/dnsbl publishes (the dnsbl/manifest feed rows, each dnsbl/feed-<name> body and the manifest metadata's group counts), out. tests/php/DnsblResourcesParityTest.php asserts today's PHP against old_expect when a case has one, else expect; go/pfb_core/dnsbl/parity_test.go asserts expect, plus refused, invalid and dropped, and refuses an old_expect equal to expect. Every old_expect is a departure the owner decided on #4036 (2026-11-23: a feed body is a sorted set) or that the plan records (section 2.4: a row the store cannot hold; a resource id is at most 128 bytes).",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "rows-already-a-sorted-set",
      "description": "Domains and ABP rules already unique and in byte order, and every feed attribute (permit mode, Custom_List provenance, the TOP1M box): both writers give the same rows, feed rows and group counts, in configuration order.",
      "feeds": [
        {
          "header": "Ads",
          "group": "AdsGroup",
          "log": "1",
          "staged": [
            "[\"a\", \"@@||ok.b.example^\"]",
            "[\"d\", \"a.example\"]",
            "[\"d\", \"b.example\"]",
            "[\"a\", \"||c.example^\"]"
          ]
        },
        {
          "header": "Allow",
          "group": "AllowGroup",
          "log": "0",
          "provenance": "user",
          "mode": "permit",
          "top1m": true,
          "staged": [
            "[\"d\", \"allow.example\"]",
            "[\"d\", \"bücher.example\"]"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "feeds": [
          {
            "feed": "Ads",
            "group": "AdsGroup",
            "logFlag": "1",
            "provenance": "feed",
            "mode": "deny",
            "top1m": false,
            "rows": [
              "@@||ok.b.example^",
              "a.example",
              "b.example",
              "||c.example^"
            ]
          },
          {
            "feed": "Allow",
            "group": "AllowGroup",
            "logFlag": "0",
            "provenance": "user",
            "mode": "permit",
            "top1m": true,
            "rows": [
              "allow.example",
              "bücher.example"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "groups": [
          {
            "name": "AdsGroup",
            "entries": 4
          },
          {
            "name": "AllowGroup",
            "entries": 2
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "rows-in-feed-order",
      "description": "Departure (owner, 2026-11-23): a body holds the rows in byte order, so the irreducible regex rules of a feed are numbered and scanned in byte order, where today's .raw keeps the feed's order.",
      "feeds": [
        {
          "header": "Regex",
          "group": "G",
          "log": "1",
          "staged": [
            "[\"a\", \"/z[0-9]+\\\\.example/\"]",
            "[\"d\", \"z.example\"]",
            "[\"a\", \"/a[0-9]+\\\\.example/\"]",
            "[\"d\", \"a.example\"]"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "feeds": [
          {
            "feed": "Regex",
            "group": "G",
            "logFlag": "1",
            "provenance": "feed",
            "mode": "deny",
            "top1m": false,
            "rows": [
              "/a[0-9]+\\.example/",
              "/z[0-9]+\\.example/",
              "a.example",
              "z.example"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "groups": [
          {
            "name": "G",
            "entries": 4
          }
        ]
      },
      "old_expect": {
        "feeds": [
          {
            "feed": "Regex",
            "group": "G",
            "logFlag": "1",
            "provenance": "feed",
            "mode": "deny",
            "top1m": false,
            "rows": [
              "/z[0-9]+\\.example/",
              "z.example",
              "/a[0-9]+\\.example/",
              "a.example"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "groups": [
          {
            "name": "G",
            "entries": 4
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a-repeated-row-counts-once",
